  193: /// Bundles everything a block renderer needs to paint a block. Passed to every
  194: /// [BlockRendererBuilder] so custom renderers get the same surface as the
  195: /// built-in ones (selection, caret, geometry, IME composition, debug overlay).
  196: ///
  197: /// Fields are intentionally the union of what each built-in renderer consumes;
  198: /// a renderer is free to ignore the ones it does not need.
  199: ///
  200: /// Row-level chrome such as the [BlockDragHandleSpec] surface is deliberately
  201: /// editor-owned and sits outside renderer output. Renderers paint block content
  202: /// only, which keeps default drag handles available to custom renderers and
  203: /// prevents nested table-cell text or inline/object controls from becoming
  204: /// sortable rows.
  205: class BlockRenderContext {
  206:   const BlockRenderContext({
  207:     required this.block,
  208:     required this.blockIndex,
